============================================================================
2. the dyadic bin identity, and the control table
============================================================================
  C_{j+1} = (C_j + G_j)/2 with G_j = sum_I dA(I) dZ(I), because
  A_L Z_L + A_R Z_R = (A Z + dA dZ)/2.  Unrolling and using
  C_0 = |A||Z| = 2^{3m} * 2^{3m+1} = 2^{6m+1} gives
      C_J = 2 + sum_{j<J} e_j,   e_j = 2^{j-J} G_j.
  m    D_m(0)   Same     Next     C_J      max e_j    identity
  1    2        2        1        3        1          2+sum e_j = C_J
  2    2        4        2        6        17/8       2+sum e_j = C_J
  3    3        1        4        5        5/4        2+sum e_j = C_J
  4    0        0        1        1        1/2        2+sum e_j = C_J
  5    0        0        0        0        7/16       2+sum e_j = C_J
  6    1        2        1        3        1          2+sum e_j = C_J
    Every row of the supplied table reproduced exactly, and the
    identity C_J = 2 + sum_j e_j holds as exact rationals.

============================================================================
3. the structure of A and Z, and where a flip-pairing stalls
============================================================================
  Z side: flipping letter i of t shifts T by +-8u_{n+i}, and
  B | 8u_{n+i}, so b_t shifts by the EXACT integer tau_i =
  8u_{n+i}/B.  Their valuations:
      tau_0: v_2 = 3 (= 3+6i)
      tau_1: v_2 = 9 (= 3+6i)
      tau_2: v_2 = 15 (= 3+6i)
      tau_3: v_2 = 21 (= 3+6i)
      tau_4: v_2 = 27 (= 3+6i)
    so Z is an affine image of a dissociated subset-sum set --
    the same shape as the depth-n residue set.
  A side: flipping letter i of s shifts P by -+8u_i, but
  B does NOT divide 8u_i for i < n, so a_s = floor(P_s/B) shifts by
  floor((P +- 8u_i)/B) - floor(P/B), which is the exact shift PLUS
  a carry that depends on P_s mod B.  Measured carry rates:
      letter 0: 56 of 4000 flips carry across a B-boundary
      letter 1: 485 of 4000 flips carry across a B-boundary
      letter 2: 153 of 4000 flips carry across a B-boundary
    The carry is exactly the information the pairing must track;
    it is NOT determined by the bin of a_s.
  e_j profile at m=3 (level : e_j), showing where the mass sits:
