4. the control, and the exact line that distinguishes
============================================================================
      m=1: A is a point mass at 0 (all 8 of them); D = 32 = 2^{5m} = 32 ; C_J = 32
      m=2: A is a point mass at 0 (all 64 of them); D = 1024 = 2^{5m} = 1024 ; C_J = 1024
      m=3: A is a point mass at 0 (all 512 of them); D = 32768 = 2^{5m} = 32768 ; C_J = 32768
  THE LINE.  For the control every P_s < B, so a_s = 0 for all s:
  the prefix list is a single atom, dA(I) is maximal along one
  dyadic path at EVERY level, and e_j is of size 2^{3m} there --
  the test e_j <= 13 fails at once.  For the true family the P_s
  fill [0,Q) because u_i = 64^i 81^{-i-1} has a nonzero HIGH half,
  which exists only because 81^{-i-1} is a nontrivial 2-adic unit.
  So any estimate must prove that the high halves floor(P_s/B)
  spread over [0,B); that single step is where 81 enters and where
  the control dies.

